<title>USA: AT&amp;T Capital names David Banks chief executive.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T Capital names David Banks chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>MORRISTOWN, N.J. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Capital on Friday said that David Banks will take over the chief executive duties from Thomas Wajnert, who will remain as chairman.</p>
<p>Banks, 54, already is a director of AT&amp;T Capital. He will relinquish his current responsibilities as a partner at Prideaux &amp; Associates Ltd, a privately held company in the U.K.; as advisor to Nomura International Plc; and as chief executive of Penna Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>AT&amp;T Capital is a privately held leasing and finance company. It was spun off from AT&amp;T Corp in October 1996.</p>
</text>
